{
  "description": "QR / pasted URIs (SPEC §8). Builders percent-encode every UTF-8 byte outside A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~ with uppercase hex, in the parameter order v, h, t (setup) or v, h, c, s (pair). Parsers trim surrounding whitespace and are strict: scheme and kind are case-sensitive, the parameter set must be exact (any order, no duplicates, no unknowns), v must be \"1\"; values may contain percent-escapes (either hex case) and the raw characters A-Za-z0-9-._~!$'()*,;:@/?= only, so a raw \"+\" (or any other character outside that set, e.g. \"#\", space, non-ASCII) is invalid, a raw \"=\" inside a value is allowed, and \"+\" never means space; decoded values must be valid UTF-8. h must be an https URL (http only for localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1]) without credentials, query or fragment. t must be at least 32 characters without control characters. c matches [A-Za-z0-9_-]{22} (b64 of 16 bytes). s is the canonical b64 of exactly 32 bytes.",
